--\u003C/span>] \u003Cbr id=\"al4-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">4\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>] \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>",{"file":583,"uri":583,"title":584,"status":585,"editions":587,"editionAuthor":45,"type":593,"objectType":594,"material":598,"condition":176,"layoutDesc":602,"handNote":606,"date":622,"places":625,"geo":628,"country":102,"provenance":99,"provenanceGeo":630,"region":112,"settlement":99,"repository":631,"textLang":632,"tmNumber":176,"facsimile":634,"letterHeights":636,"publications":645,"zotero":648,"keywords":651,"html":656,"idnoSort":156,"languageSort":115,"materialSort":599,"originSort":99,"typeSort":171},"ISic004390","Fragmentary early Christian funerary inscription",{"_":586},"edited",[588,589,590,591,592],{"type":24},{"type":26},{"type":28},{"type":31},{"type":34},{"_":171,"ana":172,"ref":173},{"_":595,"ana":596,"ref":597},"plaque","#object.plaque","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/objtyp/lod/259.html",{"_":599,"ana":228,"type":229,"subtype":600,"ref":601},"marble\n                                    ",[58],"http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/material/lod/48.html",{"layout":603},{"p":604,"rs":605,"damage":176},"Remains of three lines of Greek letters, with small space to the margin at top, and vacat to the right and a roughly consistent right margin, suggesting line ends are preserved. The letters on the fourth fragment are smaller, and preserve vacat to the left suggesting line beginning. A further line is partially preserved on the fourth fragment.",{"_":65,"ana":66,"ref":67},{"lettering":607,"dimensions":608},"The letters are fairly regularly cut, with almost no serifs/terminations to the strokes, excpt for the slight extension of the apex of alpha and delta. Alpha has broken bar; omicron is slightly ovoid and full size; pi has equal length verticals; epsilon is lunate; phi is rhomboid.",[609,611,615,617],{"type":73,"l":183,"from":91,"to":91,"h":610,"unit":